Tests run against build artifacts, never against a device.

The convention inherited from the gts9u port: every defect that was invisible
until it bit gets a check here that proves its fix on the finished artifact
(see build-rootfs-image.sh's debugfs root-inode check for the pattern — that
one lives inline because it gates the build).

Planned first entries, each blocked on its stage existing:

  check-boot-bundle.sh    headers, AVB footers and payload hashes of the two
                          boot images match the android-gki evidence output
  check-rootfs.sh         no distro kernel installed, fstab labels, conf.d
                          present, required-packages list complete
  check-release-zip.sh    the ZIP contains exactly the documented files and
                          its SHA256SUMS verifies
